+# Story 6.1: CLI Framework & Structure
+
+## Business Context
+
+This story creates the foundational CLI binary that operators will use to interact with Axiathon. Without it, there is no operator-facing command-line tool -- every subsequent CLI story (6.2-6.7) depends on the framework established here. The story delivers the `axiathon-client` crate producing the `axiathon` binary, the clap 4.x command structure with all command groups as stubs, the `SiemClient` HTTP wrapper, output formatting (table/JSON/CSV), config file loading, shell completion generation, and error-to-exit-code mapping.
+
+This is the operator's primary entry point to Axiathon. It must be learnable (organized help, examples), scriptable (JSON output, exit codes), and consistent with the docker/kubectl two-binary pattern.
+
+## Technical Guardrails
+
+- **Crate:** `crates/axiathon-client/` producing binary `axiathon`
+- **Dependency rule:** depends on `axiathon-core` ONLY for shared types. No server-side crate imports (storage, detection, ingestion, query). All data flows through HTTP via `SiemClient`.
+- **CLI framework:** clap 4.x with derive macros (`#[derive(Parser)]`, `#[derive(Subcommand)]`). Global flags defined with `global = true`.
+- **Command naming:** plural nouns with verb subcommands (`axiathon rules list`, not `axiathon rule list`). Architecture doc overrides epic AC on this point.
+- **Output formatting:** `OutputFormatter` trait with Table (comfy-table), JSON (serde_json + metadata), CSV (csv crate) implementations. Table default for TTY, JSON for piped output. Use `std::io::IsTerminal` (not deprecated `atty` crate).
+- **Credential storage:** OS keychain via `keyring` crate. Load token at CLI startup in sync context BEFORE entering Tokio runtime to avoid deadlocks. Fall back to `AXIATHON_API_TOKEN` env var for CI/CD.
+- **Config file:** `~/.config/axiathon/cli.toml` via `dirs` crate. Precedence: CLI flags > env vars > config file > defaults.
+- **Exit codes:** 0=success, 1=error, 2=usage (clap auto), 3=auth failure, 4=authz failure. Implemented via `CliError::exit_code()` method.
+
+### Key Files to Create
+
+All under `crates/axiathon-client/src/`: `main.rs`, `cli.rs`, `client.rs`, `config.rs`, `error.rs`, `output.rs`, `commands/mod.rs`, `commands/query.rs`, `commands/rules.rs`, `commands/alerts.rs`, `commands/ingest.rs`, `commands/config.rs`, `commands/status.rs`, `commands/tenant.rs`, `commands/login.rs`, `commands/completion.rs`, `commands/init.rs`.
+
+### Workspace Cargo.toml Changes
+
+Add to `[workspace.dependencies]`: `reqwest` 0.12 (json, rustls-tls), `comfy-table` 7, `keyring` 3, `clap_complete` 4, `dirs` 6, `csv` 1, `toml` 0.9.
+
+### What NOT to Touch
+
+- `axiathon-api` / `axiathon-server` crate (rename happens separately)
+- `axiathon-tui` crate (TUI code lives there, not in axiathon-client)
+- Login/auth implementation (Story 9.1)
+- Any command handler implementation beyond stubs (except completion and init which are functional)
+
+## Scope Boundaries
+
+**In scope:**
+- `axiathon-client` crate with `axiathon` binary
+- clap 4.x declarative command structure with all command groups
+- Global flags: `--format`, `--verbose`, `--quiet`, `--tenant`, `--server`, `--config`, `--no-color`
+- `OutputFormatter` trait with Table/JSON/CSV implementations
+- `SiemClient` HTTP wrapper with header injection and error mapping
+- `CliError` enum with exit code mapping
+- `ClientConfig` TOML loading with env var overrides
+- Shell completion generation (functional, not stub)
+- `axiathon init` first-time setup (functional, not stub)
+- Stub handlers for all unimplemented command groups
+
+**Out of scope:**
+- `axiathon login` implementation (Story 9.1)
+- `axiathon status` implementation (Story 6.2)
+- `axiathon config` implementation (Story 6.3)
+- `axiathon ingest` implementation (Story 6.4)
+- `axiathon alert` implementation (Story 6.5)
+- `axiathon query run` implementation (Story 5.5)
+- Dynamic shell completions from API (future enhancement)
+- `axiathon-server` crate rename (separate task)
+- TUI mode implementation (Epic 4)
+
+## AC Context
+
+**AC-1 (Top-level command groups):** `axiathon --help` must show all command groups: `query`, `rules`, `alerts`, `ingest`, `config`, `status`, `tenant`, `login`/`logout`, `tui`, `completion`, `init`. Note the plural `rules`/`alerts` per architecture doc. The `server` commands belong in the server binary, not here.
+
+**AC-2 (Subcommand help):** Every `axiathon <cmd> --help` must render without panic, show detailed help text, document all options with defaults, and include `after_help` usage examples for each command group.
+
+**AC-3 (Exit codes):** Exit codes 0/1/2/3/4 as documented. clap automatically maps usage errors to 2. Errors printed to stderr, normal output to stdout. The `CliError` enum has an `exit_code()` method; `main.rs` catches errors and calls `std::process::exit()`.
+
+**AC-4 (Output format):** `--format table|json|csv` on all tabular commands. Table auto-detects terminal width, wraps content, uses ANSI colors (disabled when non-TTY or `--no-color`). JSON includes `ResponseMetadata` (request_id, timestamp, api_version). CSV includes headers with proper escaping via `csv` crate.
+
+**AC-5 (Global flags):** All global flags defined with `global = true` in clap. `-v` is repeatable (`-vv` for debug). `--quiet` suppresses output. `--server` supports `AXIATHON_SERVER` env var.
+
+**AC-6 (Clap declarative):** Derive macros only. No imperative command building.
+
+**AC-7 (SiemClient):** `SiemClient` wraps `reqwest::Client`. Injects `X-Tenant-ID` and `Authorization: Bearer <token>` headers. Maps HTTP status codes to `CliError` variants: 401 -> AuthenticationExpired, 403 -> Unauthorized, 404 -> NotFound, 429 -> RateLimited, 5xx -> ServerError, timeout -> ConnectionTimeout, connection refused -> ServerUnavailable.
+
+**AC-8 (Config loading):** Config from `~/.config/axiathon/cli.toml`. Override path via `--config`. Env vars `AXIATHON_API_URL`, `AXIATHON_TIMEOUT` override file values. Tokens in OS keychain, NOT config file.
+
+**AC-9 (Shell completion):** `axiathon completion <shell>` generates static completions for bash/zsh/fish/PowerShell. Script to stdout, installation instructions to stderr. Uses `clap_complete::generate()`.
+
+**AC-10 (Stub handlers):** Unimplemented commands print "not yet implemented (Story X.Y)" and exit with code 1.
